# Cretli — previewing a page

To open, screenshot or debug a web page (a running app or the Cretli UI) use the
built-in Browser through the Cretli MCP tools `browser_*`, starting with
`browser_open { url }`. The user sees the same tab in the **Browser** panel.

- Do **not** launch your own Playwright/Chromium for a preview, and do not probe
  for a debug port or another browser profile.
- Never look for credentials, cookies or session tokens in `.env` or `data/`.
- When a `browser_*` call fails, report the error code; it says what the user
  has to do.

Read the `cretli-browser` skill (`.agents/skills/cretli-browser/SKILL.md`) for
the tool flow, consent cards, sign-in and performance traces.
